// Title: Member added to the local Administrators group
// Data source table: SecurityEvent
// What it detects: Windows event 4732 (a member was added to a security-enabled local group) where the
//   group is the built-in Administrators group. Attackers add an account to local administrators to
//   keep or raise privilege on a host.
// Likely false positives: IT onboarding and imaging tasks; endpoint management tools that enrol a device
//   admin group; software installers that add a service account.
// MITRE ATT&CK technique: T1098 Account Manipulation
// Tuning notes: The group is matched by its well-known SID S-1-5-32-544 so it works on any OS language.
//   MemberName is often "-" on newer Windows versions, so MemberSid is the reliable column; resolve it
//   against a watchlist of known accounts. Exclude expected change-makers (for example your management
//   service account) by SubjectUserName. Domain-level groups use different events (4728 for global and
//   4756 for universal groups); add them if you also want Domain Admins coverage.
// Status: Written against the documented SecurityEvent schema. Not yet run in a live Sentinel workspace.

let lookback = 1d;
SecurityEvent
| where TimeGenerated > ago(lookback)
| where EventID == 4732
| where TargetSid == "S-1-5-32-544"
| project
    TimeGenerated,
    Computer,
    GroupName = TargetUserName,
    GroupSid = TargetSid,
    AddedMemberName = MemberName,
    AddedMemberSid = MemberSid,
    ChangedBy = strcat(SubjectDomainName, "\\", SubjectUserName),
    SubjectLogonId
| order by TimeGenerated desc
